    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as our definitive anchor, boasting an elite 83.29 score against Emerson Hancock. The combination of a highly favorable park factor (+16%) and a strong lineup placement at the #2 spot provides him with the highest ceiling in the projected order. Alongside him, **Miguel Andujar** (67.28) and **Nolan Schanuel** (64.62) offer excellent value, both benefiting from soft matchups against Andrew Abbott and Spencer Arrighetti, respectively. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is a staple, his matchup against Cristopher S\u00e1nchez (2.74 xERA) tempers his score to 58.89, placing him on the cusp of our \"Strong\" tier; however, his lineup security and pedigree keep him locked into the 1B spot.\n\nStrategic platoon advantages are driving much of our middle-infield production today. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (60.34) and **Curtis Mead** (48.37) are both facing Logan Webb, and while Webb presents a challenging SP_xERA of 3.46, the dynamic platoon leverage (+14% and +10%) and favorable wind conditions provide just enough lift to maintain their viability. Our most difficult bench decision involved **Nasim Nunez**, whose 44.31 score fell just short of the cut. While **Nasim Nunez** brings the elite speed we prioritize in our 5x5 build, his projected #8 spot in the lineup and the specific defensive metrics of the opposing catcher penalized his efficiency score, keeping him on the pine in favor of the higher-projected **Coby Mayo** and **Curtis Mead**.\n\nWe remain cautious regarding today's \"Lineup Pending\" status for several key pieces, as the optimizer\u2019s output assumes historical batting positions that may shift once official cards are submitted. While **Kyle Tucker** and **Luis Robert Jr.** remain unavailable due to scheduling and injury, respectively, our current construction balances high-ceiling power with the calculated risk of facing mid-tier arms like Abbott and Arrighetti. We will continue to monitor the weather and any late lineup shuffling that could negatively impact **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** or **Jackson Merrill** if they slide down the order, but as it stands, the lineup is optimized to maximize both R and RBI opportunities while maintaining our competitive edge in the scarcest categories.",
